Acoustic model conversion preserves the ResembleAI, Alibaba/CosyVoice and
Matcha-TTS provenance described in ../tools/kitten-tts/README.md. Model weights
are downloaded separately and retain the model publisher's license.

The NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit is installed separately for builds. The native build
links CUDA::cudart_static and uses CMAKE_CUDA_RUNTIME_LIBRARY=Static, so its
shared library contains NVIDIA CUDA runtime code. That code retains
NVIDIA's terms; it is not Apache-2.0 material. CUDA 12.8's EULA lists
libcudart_static.a among redistributable components, subject to its distribution
requirements. Review those terms before distributing binaries:
https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/12.8.0/eula/index.html

Optional output encoders (KT2N_AV) and uploaded-audio decoding for cloning
(KT2N_VOICE_AV) link FFmpeg's libavformat, libavcodec, libswresample and libavutil.
The enabled FFmpeg build's own license and configuration apply; some builds
include GPL components. Review the actual linked libraries before distributing
a cloning-enabled shared library. See https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html
FFmpeg source is not bundled here.

Optional cloning weights retain their upstream terms. The pinned
pyannote/embedding model card declares MIT and requires accepted access through
Hugging Face. The preparation tool does not grant access or redistribute this
checkpoint. See README.md for the preparation workflow; source revisions are pinned in tools/kt2n_assets/clone_assets.py.
CPU-only export dependencies and GoogleTest retain their
upstream licenses; their source is not included in this directory.
